    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the suite, and it's green. The build passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date rule: when no registration date is supplied on owner creation, it defaults to the server's current date, and `registrationDate` is returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so it appears on both the create payload (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and the read model (`OwnerDto`). The `date` format makes the generated DTO a `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` (`LocalDate`) column with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it automatically by name.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, default `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the request omits it; a supplied date is preserved.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added a nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`), since the test profile runs with `ddl-auto=none`.\n\n5. **Seed data** \u2014 The `hsqldb` and `mysql` `data.sql` use positional `INSERT ... VALUES`, so I appended a `registration_date` value to each owners row (`h2`/`postgres` use explicit column lists and needed no change).\n\nBoth new tests pass (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`), and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
